ives 10 or 20 messages per day. There may be people who would like to subscribe to the list, but don't want to receive every message the moment it is sent. You can set up a }{\i digest}{ mail list (in this case, }{\b\f2 cars-digest}{
) which accumulates all the messages received in one day and sends them in a single message.
\par With MailSite, you create a digest mailing list that is associated with an existing MailSite mailing list. To do this, select the Mail List folder in the Console.  Select the domain containing the list y
ou want to create a digest for, and use the normal list-creation mechanism to create a new mailing list.   Assign the same name as the existing list with the word }{\b\f2 -digest}{
 appended to it. So if you want to create a digest list for an existing list called }{\b\f2 discuss}{, create a new list called }{\b\f2 discuss-digest}{. The }{\b\f2 -digest}{ postfix tells MailSite to treat the list specially.
\par As far as the mail list subscriber is concerned, the digest list can be subscribed to and unsubscribed from just like other mailing lists. For instance, to subscribe, the user would send a }{\b\f2 JOIN}{ command }{\b\f2 to discuss-digest-request@myco.com}
{.  Note that a digest mailing list must be in the same domain as the list that it digests.
\par You cannot submit messages to the digest list. Any attempt to do so will result in a non-delivery message being returned. Messages must be submitted to the main list (}{\b\f2 discuss@myco.com}{).
\par When you open the properties for a digest list in the Console, you will find that there is an extra page called }{\b\f2 Digest}{. You can use this page to control the extra properties of the digest list.
\par In the }{\uldb List General Page}{\v\uldb ListGeneralPage}{, you will find that the fields relating to list moderation have been disabled. This is because list moderation is not necessary for digests.
\par Also in the }{\uldb List General Page}{\v\uldb ListGeneralPage}{, the function of the }{\b\f2 Maximum message size}{
 field is slightly different for digest lists. If this is non-zero, then messages will be accumulated until the maximum size is reached, or the normal digest accumulation period is reached (whichever is sooner).
\par If a mail list has a digest, you can use the }{\b\f2 Members and digesters}{ radio button to specify that members of the list itself and members of the digest list may both submit messages to the list.
