Dialup support in MailSite works like this:  At regular intervals (which you can configure), MailSite dials your ISP.  Once connected, it will execute a command to request the 
ISP's mail server to send mail to MailSite.  It will also attempt to deliver outgoing mail through the normal MailSite mail routing mechanism (i.e. the DNS and the manual routing table).  If you wish, you can configure the manual routing table such that a
ll outgoing mail is routed to your ISP's mail server for it to forward--
this may help reduce the time spent connected.  When there is no more outgoing mail to send, and there are no incoming connections, the dialup connection will be closed and the phone disconnected.
