\fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\cs100\super K}{ Directory Harvest Attack Protection (DHAP) Settings}}}{\i0\cf0  Directory Harvest Attack Protection (DHAP) Settings
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
MailSite provides a mechanism for identifying a directory/dictionary harvest attack or }{\b DHA}{ (otherwise known as email harvesting) and preventing the attack from continuing for a "block duration"
 configurable in the MailSite console. When the block duration expires the host regains access but may be blocked again. 
\par When a host is deemed a harvester its IP address, host name, the time of blocking, block duration and the total number of times blocked is written to the SMTPRA log and the host is disconnected.
\par You may wish to permanently block an IP address that has been identified as a harvesting address using the "Reject all incoming mail from these hosts option" in the SMTP security dialogue or by using your firewall.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa120\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {
DHAP settings are invoked by clicking on the DHAP Settings tab in the Security Properties dialog in the MailSite admin console.
\par For more information on how to configure MailSite DHAP settings, please refer to the }{\b Windows Administration Console}{ section of this manual.
