s SMTP server from a host whose name, IP address, or }{\b\f2 EHLO}{ identification matches the }{\b\f2 Reject all incoming mail from these hosts}{ list, then all attempts by that host to transfer mail to MailSite will be rejected when the
 client issues the }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM}{ command. (Note that you should check the }{\b\f2 Lookup SMTP hosts in the DNS}{ box to get maximum benefit from this feature.)
\par If a connection comes in to MailSite from a host that does not appear in the }{\b\f2 Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts}{
 list, then MailSite will refuse to accept mail from that host for recipients other than local mailboxes, unless the destination mail domain appears in the }{\b\f2 Accept mail for relay to these domains}{ list.
\par If a }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM:}{ command is issued with an e-mail address that appears in the }{\b\f2 Reject all incoming mail from these addresses}{ list, the }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM}{ command will be rejected.
