MailSite supports three different spam-scanning policies. If spam scanning is enabled, MailSite scans appropriate messages as they arrive, and it is the associated sieve scripts that determine the action taken. Scanning can be enabled at three levels:

\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb60\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar
\jclisttab\tx720\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls154\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {\b Server-level spam scanning}{, which causes every message received by MailSite' SMTP serv
er to be scanned for potential spam.  This policy is typically used by offices, universities, and other organizations.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b Domain-level spam scanning}{, which specifies that messages should be scanned for spam only if they are sent to or from a mailbox in specif
ic domains.  This policy is typically used by mail hosting companies that wish to sell spam scanning as a value-added feature for hosted domains.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}{\b Mailbox-level spam scanning}{, which specifies that messages should be scanned for spam only if they are sent to
 or from specific mailboxes.  This policy is typically used by ISPs that wish to sell spam scanning as a value-added feature for their subscribers.
\par }\pard\plain \s31\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa100\saauto1\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Note that the domain and mailbox spam scanning policies can be used together. This means that you can configure spam scanning to occur for all mailboxes in one domain, while scanning only for selected mailboxes in a second domain.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf10\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Taking Action On Spam with Sieve Filters}{\cf0 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
While the Sophos spam-scanning engine provides the power to determine how likely it is that a given message is spam, MailSite'
s enhanced Sieve rule implementation provides administrators and end-users alike the power to implement and enforce their own personal spam policy. Actions include: reject, redirect, annotate, quarantine, and deliver. 
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf10\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {Spa
m Quarantine}{\cf0 
\par }\pard\plain \s31\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Rather than immediately discarding or rejecting messages suspected of being spam, MailSite administrators have the option of sending these messages to a special spam quarantine folder which is automatically created for each user and is located
 in each users mailbox. 
\par End-users can periodically review their spam quarantine folder to identify any false positives, which may be eliminated through a whitelisting process. This "Junk Mail" folder can be reviewed by end-users through MailSite Express o
r any standard IMAP email client.
\par End-users can also implement their own policy for sending messages to the spam quarantine. This special quarantine folder automatically purges messages every 30 days in order to avoid any over-quota concerns.
\par }\pard\plain \s3\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel2\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\i\f1\fs24\cf10\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
