The Database Mail List Plugin makes use of some default properties.  This makes it possible to create Database Mail Lists with minimal configuration.  For the default configuration, the following applies:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls144\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls144\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {An ODBC data source can be used for all dom
ains. This will need to be entered into the Mail list properties in the Database Tab of the Database Mail List.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls144\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls144\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {A separate table is used for each mail list.\~
 The name of the table must be the same as the name of the mail list, except that where the mail list name contains a dot or hyphen character.  If the list name contains a dot or hyphen you must create the table using the underscore character.\~
 This is because dot and hyphen are not legal table name characters in some databases.
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls144\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'b7}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls144\adjustright\rin0\lin720\itap0 {The table must contain at least two columns, called }{\b\f2 EmailAddress}{ and }{\b\f2 FullName.}{
   These columns must contain the e-mail addresses and names of the mail list members.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {For example, create a database mailing list called }{\b\f2 customers}{ in the virtual domain }{
\b\f2 abc.com}{.  The list address would be }{\b\f2 customers@abc.com}{.\~ To map this to a database, create a data source called }{\b\f2 abc.com}{ and a table }{\b\f2 customers}{ in this data source.  The table }{\b\f2 customers}{ must have columns }{
\b\f2 EmailAddress}{ and }{\b\f2 FullName}{.
\par An example of using the Database Mail List Plugin is provided in the appendix on }{\uldb Database Examples}{\v\uldb DatabasePluginExamples}{.
\par 
