{\b\f2 Map From}{ field. This can be used to redirect mail for all names matching a pattern. For instance, specifying a user name of }{\b\f2 t*y}{ would match }{\b\f2 Tony}{, }{\b\f2 Tiny}{, }{\b\f2 toby}{, }{\b\f2 terry}{
, etc. (Note that matching is not case sensitive.)
\par You can also specify a single wildcard as the first character of the }{\b\f2 Map To}{ field. This will be replaced by the actual user name when the table entry is used. For instance, if the }{\b\f2 Map From}{ string is }{\b\f2 f*}{ and the corresponding }
{\b\f2 Map To}{ string is }{\b\f2 *-blue@xyz.com}{, then a message for }{\b\f2 fred@abc.com}{ will be redirected to }{\b\f2 fred-blue@xyz.com}{.
\par This feature can be used to redirect all mail for one domain to a second domain.  The second domain could be local to this machine, or on a remote machine.  This is done by specifying a }{\b\f2 Map From}{ string of }{\b\f2 *@abc.com}{ and a  }{\b\f2 
Map To}{ string of }{\b\f2 *@xyz.com}{.
