rver Agent for every message that is received.  The agent is passed the names of two files: the message file itself, and a file containing SMTP envelope information.
\par The }{\i message file}{ is a text file with a }{\b\f2 MSG}{ extension.  The file containing the SMTP envelope information is known as the }{\i recipients file}{
, although it contains more than just recipient information. The recipients file is a text file with a }{\b\f2 RCO}{ extension when it is passed to the Server Agent.  When the agent terminates, MailSite will rename the file to its normal }{\b\f2 RCP}{
 extension.
\par This field should contain a command-line template.  An occurrence of }{\b\f2 %r}{ in the template is replaced by the name of the recipients file, and an occurrence of }{\b\f2 %m}{ in the template is replaced by the name of the message file.  T
he resulting command line is then passed to the command-line interpreter to execute.
\par Thus, if the template were:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs20 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li1080\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls60\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'de}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls60\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2 copy "%r" c:\\temp & copy "%m" c:\\temp
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {MailSite would copy both the message file and the recipients file to the }{\b\f2 c:\\temp}{
 directory.
\par Multiple commands can be executed, as in the above example, by separating each command with the }{\b\f2 &}{ character (or by using a batch file).
\par The agent is executed by the SMTPRA service and agent inherits the access rights of the SMTPRA service.  If you installed MailSite to run its services as a specific Windows user, you must grant this user execute access for the agent application.
\par It is important that the Server Agent should not take too long to execute.  Otherwise, a busy mail server could easily run out of memory or saturate its processor.
\par It is possible for the Server Agent to delete or move the message file and recipients files - for instance if the agent determines that the message contains a virus.  In this case, the agent should respect the wishes of the sender rega
rding delivery status notifications, as expressed in the recipients file.  This means that the agent may need to send a Delivery Status Notification message. Not to do so may be a violation of the SMTP protocol.
