MailSite can be configured to perform a reverse lookup of the IP address of the incoming SMTP host.  The resulting host name is used in the log files and in the }{\b\f2 Received:}{
 header.  If the reverse lookup fails then connection is rejected unless the }{\b\f2 Accept Unknown Hosts}{ option is turned on.
\par This option can help block unauthorized SMTP relay because many junk mail distributors do not have a valid reverse DNS record.
\par This option can have a serious impact on performance.  MailSite must submit a reverse DNS lookup query for each incoming connection.  If your DNS server is slow then incoming connections may experience significant delays.
