Checking this box is a quick way to stop your mail server being used to relay spam to other sites.  If you check this, then MailSite will not accept mail for relay unless the }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM:}{
 address in the SMTP envelope refers to a local domain.  (Note that the }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM:}{ address specifies the return address for non-delivery reports - it is not necessarily the same as the }{\b\f2 From:}{ address in the message header.)
\par This option will not protect your mail server against determined spammers, who are capable of forging the }{\b\f2 MAIL FROM:}{ address.  You can get better protection using the }{\b Require SMTP authentication for relaying}{ option, or through the }{\b 
Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts}{ mask list.  (Note that if you set up the }{\b Accept mail for relay from these friendly hosts}{ list, you should turn off this option since it overrides the value in that field.)
