A mask list works as follows.  A host name (or IP address, domain name or e-mail address, depending on the list in question) either matches
 or does not match the list.  The host name is tested against each mask in the list in turn, starting from the top.  If it fits the mask, this is treated as a match, unless the mask is preceded by an exclamation point (meaning "exclude from the list"
).  This is treated as a failure to match the list, and no further masks in the list will be examined. If the end of the list is reached without a match being found, the host name is deemed not to match the list.
