\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
A delivery attempt for each outstanding mail domain (other than domains in the }{\b\f2 Exclude Domains}{
 field) will be made every time a dialup connection is established. If the delivery attempt is unsuccessful (for example, if the remote mail server is down or inaccessible at the scheduled dialup time), MailSite wil
l retain the message and retry later. However, if the number of delivery attempts exceeds a preset limit, delivery will be abandoned and a non-delivery notification will be generated. This field sets the limit for the number of attempts. The default value
 is 20.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\f2\fs20\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
\lang2057\langfe1033\langnp2057 Incoming Delivery trigger command
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
When it is time for a delivery attempt to be made, before doing anything else, MailSite will execute the }{\b\f2 Delivery Trigger Command}{.  This can be any command you specify, but often it will be either the }{\b\f2 MSSTART}{ or the }{\b\f2 MSPOP}{
 command, which can be used to request your Internet Service Provider's mail server to deliver queued messages to MailSite.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {
Once connected to your ISP it is often necessary to take some action to cause your ISP's mail server to start sending your mail.  For instance, some ISP's let you use a }{\b\f2 finger}{ command.  Others (such as MailSite itself) will respond to an }{
\b\f2 ETRN}{ SMTP command. If your ISP's mail server needs prompting in this way, check this box and type in the command line to execute. The command line can either invoke a program or a batch file.  You must specify the full path.
\par If your ISP's mail server understands the }{\b\f2 ETRN}{ command, you could use the }{\b\f2 MSSTART}{ command to trigger delivery of queued mail for your domain:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs18 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li1080\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls63\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'de}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls63\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\fs18 C:\\Program Files\\MailSite\\msstart -h mailserver.isp.com myco.com
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {This tells the mail server to start sending mail for }{\b\f2 myco.com}{.
\par Alternatively, your ISP may accumulate mail for you in a mailbox, and expect you to download it using POP. The }{\b\f2 MSPOP}{ utility will help in this situation. }{\b\f2 MSPOP}{ w
ill retrieve mail from the mailbox at your ISP and will redirect it to recipients on your local system. You might type in the following trigger command line:
\par {\pntext\pard\plain\f3\fs18 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'de\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-720\li1080\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\jclisttab\tx1080\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640{\*\pn \pnlvlblt\ilvl0\ls64\pnrnot0
\pnf3\pnstart1\pnindent360\pnsp120\pnhang{\pntxtb \'de}}\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\ls64\adjustright\rin0\lin1080\itap0 {\b\f2\fs18 C:\\Program Files\\MailSite\\mspop -h mailserver.isp.com -u myusername -p mypassword
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 {Note that when c
alculating the duration of the dialup connection, MailSite will not start counting until the Delivery Trigger Command (if it exists) has finished. Thus, a command that does not terminate could cause the dialup connection to stay open indefinitely.
