 Domains,Default}}}{The default domain can be identified by the gray folder icon.  This is the "home" domain for this server.  MailSite reads the name of the default domain from the }{\b\f2 HOST}{ and }{\b\f2 DOMAIN}{
 fields in your TCP/IP: DNS configuration. 
\par The default domain always exists--you cannot delete it.  However, the default domain name can be changed.  For example, if MailSite was installed with the default domain }{\b\f2 mail.mycompany.com}{ , you can change this to be }{\b\f2 mycompany.com}{.

\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\f2\fs20\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
