To rename the default domain, select the domain, then click on the domain name. Or, select the domain and select }{\b\f2 Rename}{ from the right-button pop-up menu.
\par If you rename the default domain, it is your responsibility to ensure that the new domain name has an appropriate MX record in the DNS, so that mail addressed to }{\b\f2 user@mucompany.com}{ gets routed to the mail server at }{\b\f2 mail.mycompany.com}{.

\par You can only rename the default domain.  To rename other domains, create a new domain, move the users and mailing lists from the old domain into the new one, then delete the old domain.
\par }\pard\plain \s4\ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\outlinelevel3\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \b\f2\fs20\ul\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
