\par If you associate the virtual domain with an IP address, then the DNS record for this domain must resolve to this IP address.  In addition, users must use this DNS address as their 
SMTP and POP3 server. In this case, POP3 and IMAP4 users can log in with their simple name, such as }{\b\f2 joe}{, or with their fully qualified name, such as }{\b\f2 joe@abc.com}{.
