There is a second record type is called Mail eXchange (MX) records.  These records are devoted to the delivery of mail. A MX record for a particular 
name will have several addresses and priorities. For example, to send e-mail to DEC, you need to use the name }{\b\f2 dec.com}{. DEC has the following MX records, each with a different priority number:
