\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
These records tell mail software where to send the mail and what to do if the first machine is not available. If the mail server }{\b\f2 inet-gw-2.pa.dec.com}{ is being rebooted, a mail server will send mail to }{\b\f2 inet-gw-3.pa.dec.com}{
 (since these are the entries with the next higher priority in the MX record).
\par Many destinations do not have MX records. In this case, mail software will attempt to use the A instead.  Mail will be held until it is possible forward if none of these machines are available.
