<key> ::= <openingmarker>[<value>..][<subkey>..]<closingmarker>\line <openingmarker> ::= "["<escapedkeyname>"]"\line <closingmarker> ::= "[""/"<escapedkeyname>"]"\line <escapedkeyname> ::= key name, control chars, %, / [ and ] chars replaced by %xx \line 
<value> ::= <valuename> "=" <valuedata>\line <valuename> ::= value name with any control chars, % and = chars replaced by %xx\line <valuedata> ::= <dwordvaluedata>|<stringvaluedata>|<multistringvaluedata>\line <dwordvaluedata> ::= string of decimal digits
\line <stringvaluedata> ::= '"'[<stringdata>]'"'\line <stringdata> ::= sequence of chars with any control chars, % and " replaced by %xx\line <multistringvaluedata> ::= <stringvaluedata>[<stringvaluedata>..]'"''"'\line <subkey> ::= <key>
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li360\ri0\sb60\sa60\widctlpar\tx2880\tx3600\tx4320\tx5040\tx5760\tx6480\tx7200\tx7920\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin360\itap0 \fs20\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {
Note that an empty multistring is represented as }{\b\f2 "" ""}{ whereas an empty string is represented as }{\b\f2 ""}{.\~ It is vital that the opening and closing markers and each value are on a line by themselves - i.e. no newlines within }{\b\f2 
<openmarker>}{, }{\b\f2 <closemarker>}{ or }{\b\f2 <value>}{.
\par You can backup the MailSite configuration at any time.\~ However, it is important to stop all services before restoring the configuration.
