The Emerald software contains a Radius server for validating access to the network. The Radius server uses a Microsoft SQL Server 
database containing user information. If you select the Emerald Radius Server Database option in the database mailbox plugin, the plugin will use the Emerald database for mailbox authentication.
\par The database mailbox plugin does not contain detailed knowledge of the Emerald database schema. All access to the database is performed by calling }{\i stored procedures}{. Two stored procedures are used:  }{\b\f2 VerifyMailUser}{ and }{\b\f2 
ListMailUsers}{. These are shipped as part of the Emerald release 2.5 and RadiusNT release 2.5.  If you do not have them, you should approach IEA-Software (supplier of the Emerald and RadiusNT packages) to obtain them.
